t in 2026 after Andy Barr left the House to run for Senate. The district leans Republican by about seven points, and most professional race ratings call it Likely Republican, though several rate it Lean Republican. Republican Ralph Alvarado, a physician and former state senator, faces Democrat Zach Dembo, a Lexington attorney. Both have raised roughly $1.5 million, with Dembo holding slightly more cash and drawing more outside support.\n\nPolling in the race has come entirely from Democratic sponsors, and the most recent survey in late August showed a one-point Democratic edge, with earlier polls essentially tied. Prediction markets give Republicans about a 74 percent chance. A proxy war of ads tied to Governor Andy Beshear and Trump-linked groups has drawn national attention and kept Democrats engaged, but the district's partisan lean still favors Alvarado heading into November.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2515, "margin": -3.92}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.296, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2877, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2982, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.223, "margin": -4.5}]}